{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Outsourcing to the Cloud: Data Security and Privacy Risks "}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.3"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use when talking about data security and privacy risks. "}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about people's backgrounds in spoken or written documents.  Interpret the IT needs assessment, to determine the required technology to manage information, according to the rules and protocols established by the company. "}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of a range of grammar and vocabulary, and with the appropriate level of formality and purpose, coherence and cohesion for the context.   Recognizes simple ideas on concepts on IT contracts and knowledge transfer, simulated processes of IT contracting, and technological negociation."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Negative Questions to Suggest an Idea"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use <b>questions in negative form</b> to suggest ideas and encourage somebody to agree with us. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Negative questions are used when you expect another person to agree with your idea or when you want to confirm what you are saying. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:</br><i> <b>Don't you</b> need to read all the contract?</i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember that we can use negative questions in different tenses and by using different verbs. Whenever we express an idea in a simple tense and the main verb of the sentence is different from the verb <b>to be</b>, we are doing to use the verb <b>to do</b> as an auxiliary."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:</br><i><b> Don't </b>you need to outsource data to your cloud?</i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Companies have incorporated cloud computing into their service. Don't you think we should try to do the same in our business?  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We should go over the principals and policies for signing with a cloud provider. Don't you agree it's better to be informed beforehand?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "However, when the man verb of the sentence is the verb to be, we are not going to use any auxiliary verb."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:</br><i> You'd better leave now, <b>aren't</b> you supposed to show the results at the meeting? </i>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Inseparable Phrasal Verbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<b>Inseparable phrasal verbs</b>, just as its name suggest, are phrasal verbs whose verb and preposition or adjective go next to each other. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "When using<b> inseparable phrasal verbs</b>, the object pronoun goes after the verb. It is not possible to place a word between the verb and the preposition."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For instance, the phrasal verb <b><i>get through</i></b>, which means get over something or deal with a situation, is an inseparable phrasal verb and <b>get</b> will always be next to <b>through</b>.  "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example: </br><i>The company can't <b>get through</b> our losses. </i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "It is the same case for <b>get around to</b> which means to start doing something that was planned. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:</br><i> I am <b>getting around to</b> talking to the manager about the outsourcing data. </i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "We should go over the principals and policies for signing with a cloud provider."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are some steps to get through possible issues and minimize risks. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Some companies just don't get around to analyzing how data is treated in the cloud or they don't get down to signing detailed contracts that ensure data protection.  "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "outsource "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to transfer something to another market"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Don't you think we should discuss some specific considerations when outsourcing data to the cloud?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob02aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "clear out any doubts "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to make sure a subject or agreement is fully understood by everyone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Organizations must clear out any doubts. There is no space for bad service like data being unavailable. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob02aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "vet "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to  check or evaluate something or someone"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Additionally, it's crucial to vet the vendor. Don't you think they could steal information?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob02aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "reputational \t\t"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "how something is perceived by others"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This is very important for businesses in Europe which are concerned of the reputational impact of data breach."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob02aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "breach \t\t"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an infraction of a contract "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This is very important for businesses in Europe which are concerned of the reputational impact of data breach."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n7le02ob02aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of key considerations to outsource data to the cloud."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write examples of the negative consequences of not following such considerations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss your list with the class, be ready to ask and answer questions."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I recognize effective ways to talk minimize risks when negotiating outsourcing data to the cloud."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I enumerate important considerations when outsourcing data to the cloud."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I debate about key considerations to outsource data to the cloud"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n7le02ob02re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n7le02ob02re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<b>Lucas</b>: Companies have incorporated cloud computing into their service. Don't you think we should try to do the same in our business?  </br>\n<b>Julieta</b>: Absolutely! We should go over the principals and policies for signing with a cloud provider. Don't you agree it's better to be informed beforehand? </br>\n<b>Lucas</b>: Indeed. There are some steps to get through possible issues and minimize risks. First, we should go over the cloud-based outsourcing model to see if it suits the data we want to upload.  </br>\n<b>Julieta</b>: Don't you think we should understand how data flows in the cloud too?</br>\n<b>Lucas</b>: Sure! Some companies just don't get around to analyzing how data is treated in the cloud or they don't get down to signing detailed contracts that ensure data protection.  A cloud provider must guarantee the best practice in data security by denying any unauthorized access to private data and make sure that clients' data is backed up."}, {"time": "56000", "image": "enpe8n7le02ob02re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<b>Julieta</b>: We should definitely sign a solid contract with the cloud provider; it could be tough for us to get through data losses.  </br>\n<b>Lucas</b>: I agree, don't you think we should discuss some specific considerations when outsourcing data to the cloud?</br>\n<b>Julieta</b>: 100%. One consideration is to know the data. The rights of data access are guaranteed by the government data protection law. That's why organizations should be their own host data in the cloud. </br>\n<b>Lucas</b>: Additionally, it's crucial to vet the vendor. Don't you think they could steal information?</br>\n<b>Julieta</b>: Maybe! We must choose sophisticated services that will ensure data protection and include additional regulatory compliance issues that the outsourcing company should answer for."}, {"time": "106000", "image": "enpe8n7le02ob02re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<b>Lucas</b>: Besides, don't you think data security is key in any arrangement?</br>\n<b>Julieta</b>: Totally! In case there is an intrusion, European data protection focuses on the organization, not on the cloud vendor. This is very important for businesses in Europe, which are concerned with the reputational impact of data breach.</br>\n<b>Lucas</b>: Finally, don't you think negotiating appropriate service levels is essential? </br>\n<b>Julieta</b>: Yes. Organizations must clear out any doubts. There is no space for bad service like data being unavailable."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n7le02ob02re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about minimizing risks when negotiating outsourcing data to the cloud."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can list some considerations to outsource data to the cloud."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can exchange information about key considerations to outsource data to the cloud. "}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Have you or someone you know ever had problems when uploading your information to a cloud?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What do you think companies should consider when uploading their data to a cloud?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner:"}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Negotiating Cloud Contracts!"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0}, {"stimuli_ids": [1], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "STI", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Talking About Data Security and Privacy Risks"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_